WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- A real script organizes commands into FUNCTIONS, one per logical section
- main() at the bottom calls every function in order — easy to read, easy to extend
- Adding a new check later just means adding ONE new function + one call in main()
- printf '=%.0s' {1..50} is a trick to print a repeated character divider line
- This script combines knowledge from Day 1 (system info), Day 4/22 (processes),
  Day 5 (network), Day 10 (disk), Day 12-13 (scripting structure)
- Functions must be DEFINED before they're called (bash reads top to bottom)

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
